## STRUCT / ENUM CROSS-MODULE EDGES
Fixtures: `/tmp/r2_peer2_struct/`.

| Case | rc / key line | Note |
|------|---------------|------|
| Struct def in lib; field use + call in importer | OK | multi type floor |
| Wrong arg type to imported fn (`sum_pt(1)`) | ERR expects Point got Int | good |
| Nested struct field `o.inner.n` cross-module | OK | good |
| Annotated let init type mismatch cross-module | ERR Int vs String | good |
| Call arity cross-module | ERR expects 2 got 1 | good |
| Undefined imported name | ERR undefined variable | good |
| Struct lit field mistype `Point { x: "no", y: 2 }` multi | **OK** | **silent accept** |
| Same struct lit mistype **single-file** | **OK** | not multi-specific |
| Duplicate `struct Dup` in two imports | **OK** | silent merge residual |
| `pub enum Color { Red, Blue }` | ERR undefined `enum` | no product enum |
| Type-alias `type Color = Int` cross-module | OK | alias only |

**Honesty:** R2 multi-import TC floor covers **calls / arity / some ann types /
undefined**. It does **not** cover struct-literal field typing or duplicate type
definitions. Product **enum** is residual (keyword not wired).

Prior `/tmp/r2_*` swarm fixtures: fail-arg and undef behave; `r2_test` fails on
missing `return` for Point body form (syntax/return residual), not import load.

